id: pm-rl-qhz2
title: System One decision-model calibration adapter for the recursive loop
description: "A real bounded decision-model trainer for the recursive loop: a per-question calibration head (temperature plus per-option bias over a frozen System One decision model) served at a configurable TypeSafe-compatible endpoint POST {baseURL}/v1/systemone via plain fetch (no new runtime dependency). Environments label synthetic pm items (item type routing) from datasets with known outcomes. Each generation collects real decisions from the endpoint, fits the head with real gradient descent on the collected batch (parameters change across generations, changing the content-addressed checkpoint), evaluates on a strictly disjoint held-out split through the existing Hoeffding promotion gate, and the promoted successor collects the next generation. Held-out decisions and collected decisions are persisted per-query as merge-safe run metric events, so resume never re-queries a persisted index and never double-spends tokens. Contamination (held-out ids leaking into training) and invalid checkpoints (NaN, shape mismatch, tampered hash) stop promotion. Unit tests drive the adapter through a real in-process deterministic HTTP server; fetch is never mocked."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: execution,llm-adapter,recursive-training
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:32:35.578Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T09:36:01.246Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-glm
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "A systemone loop config parses and validates disjoint labelled datasets, question specs and decision-model endpoint bounds; the head fit performs real gradient updates so candidate checkpoints differ from their source across two generations; generation two's collection run records generation one's promoted candidate as its collecting policy; collected and held-out decisions persist as one merge-safe metric event per endpoint query and resume appends only the missing suffix; an invalid checkpoint (NaN, shape mismatch, tampered digest) or an overlapping dataset identity stops promotion with a stable refusal; the endpoint client refuses non-200 responses, malformed bodies and missing answers as expected CLI errors and honours AbortSignal and timeout; unit coverage of the adapter is exact 100/100/100/100 against a real in-process HTTP server"
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T05:05:21.442Z",codex-sol,"Preserving the interrupted calibration-head implementation in a focused commit. Typecheck and eslint pass; existing loop regressions pass 33/33. Adapter tests, endpoint acceptance and exact coverage are still pending. Audit found lease-recovery races and replay budget/refusal gaps to repair before claiming durability."
  "2026-10-05T05:38:50.425Z",codex-sol,"Second live acceptance PASS with unchanged real calibration results: accuracy 1.0 -> 1.0; ECE 0.3329814443 -> 0.2927389850 -> 0.2411651910; generation means 0.66375 -> 0.70685 and 0.709475 -> 0.761025; 1094 tokens across 8 requests. Endpoint-only elapsed 23302.17 ms, mean 2912.77 ms/request; controller wall 26157.71 ms. Generation-two source is the promoted 77bb31851756 checkpoint and successor a66accd456bf differs. Follow-up pm-rl-9nlg records the unresolved remote-completion/local-receipt kill window. Exact-source coverage remains in progress."
  "2026-10-05T06:00:38.024Z",codex-sol,"Packed npm/Node and Bun consumers both passed a real HTTP two-generation programme: two promotions, eight queries, eight charged logical samples, distinct checkpoints, successor collection attributed to generation one, read-only status and terminal resume with zero additional queries. Adapter unit tests use real in-process HTTP servers; no fetch mock or new runtime dependency. Bun check/build:test/docstring and the full npm release gate are being finalized."
  "2026-10-05T06:05:08.307Z",codex-sol,"Final release gate passed exact four-metric 100% across all 23 authored source files and 387 tests without skips. PM-linked adapter tests passed 6/6 with real HTTP servers. Bun check/build:test/docstring passed; packed npm/Node and native Bun each passed two-generation promotion, successor collection, checkpoint validation, status and no-query terminal resume. Frozen-model calibration and two-item adaptive validation limits are documented."
  "2026-10-05T06:09:57.336Z",codex-sol,"Draft PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/62 contains the calibration adapter, contamination/checkpoint guards and measured live evidence. Final packaged npm/Node and Bun acceptance both pass. Provider receipt/idempotency follow-up pm-rl-9nlg remains open. Claim released for verification."
  "2026-10-05T09:32:09.114Z",codex-sol,"Verified review 4182506941: response usage accepts fractional and unsafe token counts that durable replay rejects. Validate both counts and their sum as non-negative safe integers at the HTTP response boundary; add fractional and overflow regressions."
  "2026-10-05T09:34:48.847Z",codex-sol,"The new real HTTP regression reproduced the original bug: fractional input_tokens=10.5 was accepted. Response validation now rejects fractional or unsafe input/output counts and safe-count sums that overflow; zero usage and the maximum safe total remain accepted."
  "2026-10-05T09:36:01.246Z",codex-sol,"HTTP adapter tests PASS: node --test test/systemone.test.ts (7 tests) and node --test --test-name-pattern=\"real HTTP usage\" test/systemone.test.ts, both run via pm test pm-rl-qhz2 --run --progress. Fractional input/output counts, unsafe individual counts and overflowing totals reject with systemone_endpoint_usage_invalid; zero and maximum safe totals pass. Full release check pending."
